<article class="env-lemma" id="04HV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04HV">Lemma <span data-tag="04HV">59.31.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a subsheaf of the final object of the étale topos of $S$ (see Sites, Example <a href="/tag/00W3" data-tag="00W3">7.10.2</a>). Then there exists a unique open $W \subset S$ such that $\mathcal{F} = h_ W$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The condition means that $\mathcal{F}(U)$ is a singleton or empty for all $\varphi : U \to S$ in $\mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (S_{\acute{e}tale})$. In particular local sections always glue. If $\mathcal{F}(U) \not= \emptyset $, then $\mathcal{F}(\varphi (U)) \not= \emptyset $ because $\{ \varphi : U \to \varphi (U)\} $ is a covering. Hence we can take $W = \bigcup _{\varphi : U \to S, \mathcal{F}(U) \not= \emptyset } \varphi (U)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>